  "notes": [
    "D1 oracle is the official SL Spårtrafikkarta PNG (file SL_Spartrafikkarta_250414.png) linked from sl.se/reseplanering/kartor/spartrafikkartor as “All spårtrafik”. Stations arrays are hand-transcribed from that passenger map. Not generated from GTFS.",
    "sl.se in 2026 does not publish a separate Tunnelbana PDF or Pendeltåg PDF on the spårtrafik index; the combined rail PNG is the official printed network. Local-rail/tram get their own PNGs on the same page (out of v1).",
    "City stays planned. Modes v1: TRAIN-like rail the rider thinks of as Next Train = Tunnelbana (metro, T 10/11/13/14/17/18/19) AND Pendeltåg (40/41/43/48). Buses out. Spårväg City, Tvärbanan, Nockebybanan, Lidingöbanan, Roslagsbanan, Saltsjöbanan are on the same official map but later (hazard pack).",
    "Timezone Europe/Stockholm HAS DST (CET/CEST). Do not copy Brisbane no-DST.",
    "Passenger product on the map is colour family + line number + terminus (Blå linjen 10 Hjulsta; Röda linjen 13 Norsborg; Pendeltåg 40 Uppsala C). Recommend line + terminus. See direction-model-memo.md.",
    "LOCKED inner-city printed names from the map: T-Centralen is the metro node. Stockholm City is the pendeltåg Citybanan node. They are DIFFERENT stops (walking interchange capsule on the map). Do not collapse them. Do not emit Stockholm Central / Stockholm C / Stockholms central as the metro or pendeltåg stop. Stockholms central is the SJ/fjärrtåg station (SL Transport site 9000).",
    "Map prints Odenplan as the green-line/pendeltåg interchange. SL Transport sites split Odenplan (9117, metro) vs Stockholm Odenplan (1079, pendeltåg). Lock map word Odenplan for metro; keep Stockholm Odenplan as the pendeltåg printed/API string — do not merge the two site ids.",
    "Map prints Arlanda central (airplane). SL Transport site name Arlanda central. GTFS clash: Arlanda Centralstation. Do not use Arlanda C as the lock if the map says Arlanda central.",
    "Green 18 on the map is drawn Hässelby strand–Farsta strand. Live SL Transport at T-Centralen often shows 18 turning at Alvik; treat Alvik as a nested short, not a different D1 line.",
    "Pendeltåg 43X is a skip-stop/short of 43 (Kallhäll–Nynäshamn). Not a separate map colour. Lines 42 and 44 exist as empty-name TRAIN rows in SL Transport /lines but were withdrawn from the passenger timetable (15 Dec 2024) and are not D1 rows on the 250414 map.",
    "Line 48 Gnesta–Södertälje centrum does not run through Stockholm City. Connection at Södertälje hamn toward the rest of the network.",
    "Swedish characters must be preserved (T-Centralen, Södertälje, Hässelby, Mörby, Åkeshov, Älvsjö, Östermalmstorg, Västerhaninge). Göteborg is not in this city.",
    "Hagsätra branch is still green on this 250414 map (future blue takeover is not in-service on the oracle).",
    "Arenastaden / Hagastaden / Södra Hagalund green extension: under construction, not a D1 in-service row.",
    "gtfsRouteIdsIfKnown are Samtrafiken SL route_id values from the public ResRobot zip (agency SL). H2 names only. No stopIds in this file. Trafiklab GTFS Sweden was 403 without a key and is marked incomplete as that product."
  ],
